    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/31": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Graduate Enrollment Coordinator Enrollment Management Administration - Abilene, Texas Position Summary McMurry University seeks a dynamic, results-oriented Graduate Enrollment Professional to lead recruitment and marketing efforts for new and growing graduate programs, particularly in Business and Kinesiology. This position plays a critical role in launching, growing, and sustaining high-demand graduate programs through strategic recruitment initiatives, corporate partnerships, and personalized student engagement. The successful candidate will combine relationship-building, marketing insight, and enrollment management expertise to drive measurable growth in graduate enrollment. Primary Responsibilities Graduate Recruitment & Enrollment Growth Develop and execute a strategic recruitment plan to grow enrollment in graduate programs in Business and Kinesiology. Identify, cultivate, and convert prospective students through proactive outreach (phone, email, virtual meetings, in-person events). Represent the university at recruitment events, conferences, graduate fairs, and corporate sites. Manage the full enrollment funnel from inquiry to matriculation. Maintain consistent follow-up with prospective students to increase yield rates. Corporate & Community Partnerships Establish and grow partnerships with corporations, healthcare systems, school districts, athletic organizations, and regional employers. Negotiate cohort agreements, tuition partnerships, and employer-sponsored enrollment opportunities. Conduct on-site presentations and information sessions for corporate partners. Collaborate with university leadership to create customized graduate pathways aligned with workforce needs. Application & Admissions Management Manage graduate applications from submission through admission decision. Ensure timely collection and review of application materials. Communicate admissions decisions and next steps clearly and professionally. Maintain accurate and up-to-date records within the university’s CRM and student information system. Marketing & Outreach Collaborate with Marketing to develop targeted campaigns (digital, print, and event-based). Promote graduate programs to current McMurry undergraduate students through classroom visits, events, and direct outreach. Assist with developing recruitment materials and program messaging. Support open houses, virtual information sessions, and campus visit programs. Graduate Assistantship Support Assist in administering the Graduate Assistant program. Communicate opportunities and eligibility requirements to prospective and current students. Coordinate with program directors on GA placements and tracking. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree (Master’s preferred). 2+ years of experience in recruitment, enrollment management, sales, marketing, or corporate partnership development. Strong interpersonal and networking skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to meet enrollment, sales, or performance targets. Willingness to travel regionally and occasionally out of state. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends for recruitment events. Preferred Experience in higher education graduate recruitment. Familiarity with CRM systems (Slate, Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar). Experience building corporate or community partnerships. Knowledge of graduate program structures and adult learner markets. Core Competencies Strategic Enrollment Planning Relationship Building & Corporate Development Sales & Persuasive Communication Organization & Detail Management Data Tracking & CRM Utilization Initiative & Self-Direction Performance Expectations Growth in graduate program inquiries and applications Increase in enrolled graduate students Development of new corporate partnerships Application processing efficiency and responsiveness Graduate student yield and retention metrics Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department Enrollment Management Administration Employment Type Full-Time Minimum Experience Mid-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/38": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Adjunct Faculty Pool Human Resources - Abilene, Texas (Hybrid) Position Summary McMurry University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to support instructional needs across academic programs. This posting is used to build a pool of qualified candidates for part-time, temporary teaching assignments as they become available. Appointments are made on a course-by-course basis and are dependent upon departmental needs, enrollment, and funding. Adjunct faculty members play a vital role in delivering high-quality instruction and supporting student success. Selected candidates may teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in their area of expertise, either in-person, online, or hybrid formats. Key Areas of interest (but not limited to): Chemistry Business History Political Science Key Responsibilities Teach assigned courses in alignment with approved curriculum and learning outcomes Prepare course materials, syllabi, and instructional content Engage students through effective teaching strategies and timely communication Assess student learning and provide meaningful feedback Maintain accurate records of attendance, grades, and course activities Adhere to university policies and academic standards Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in the teaching discipline or a related field (minimum 18 graduate hours in the discipline) Relevant professional or teaching experience Strong communication and organizational skills Preferred Qualifications Prior college-level teaching experience Experience with online or hybrid instruction Terminal degree in the discipline (where applicable) Application Requirements Completed application Curriculum Vitae (CV) or resume Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Additional Information This is a continuous posting used to establish a pool of qualified applicants Applications are reviewed on an as-needed basis Submission of an application does not guarantee employment Adjunct faculty are hired on a per-course, part-time basis Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas (Hybrid) Department Human Resources Employment Type Part-Time Minimum Experience Entry-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/41": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings S-STEM Peer Mentor S3C - Abilene, Texas Preferred Availability: 10 hours per week. Each Mentor will work with their mentee in the fall and spring semesters to provide advice, support, and knowledge to the mentee as assigned by project staff. Mentors should be available to their mentee the full 10 hours each week, this may be face-to-face, via email or via call/text. Although face-to-face is preferred. Mentors will also be required to attend mentor training with other peer mentors working in the S3C. There will be a half-day training session prior to the beginning of the fall semester (or Spring as needed) with additional 1-hour meetings scheduled bi-weekly throughout the academic year. This is a two-year position, and a successful applicant will have a STEM major matched to their mentee. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department S3C Employment Type Part-Time Minimum Experience Entry-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
