    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/79": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Chapel Band Worship Leader Religious Life - Abilene, Texas Reporting to the Director of Religious & Spiritual Life, the Chapel Band Worship Leader will provide musical and spiritual leadership for McMurry University’s Chapel services. This role focuses on fostering a worshipful environment that enhances the spiritual life of the campus community. The Worship Leader will oversee the planning, preparation, and delivery of worship music in collaboration with the University Chaplains and student musicians. Part-Time (6-8 Hours per Week) | 10 Month Contract (Mid-August through Mid-May) Duties & Responsibilities : Chapel Band Worship Leader will take primary responsibility for the following: Coordinate & Lead Weekly Chapel Band Rehearsal Lead student musicians in planning & preparing music for Chapel Lead rehearsal, including support of student musicians in Chapel Band to develop student leadership through both musical and spiritual growth Recruit, welcome, and integrate new student musicians into Chapel Band in coordination with Religious & Spiritual Life Staff Coordinate setup of portable sound system and necessary equipment during or prior to rehearsal Plan & Lead Worship Music for Weekly Chapel Services (Tuesdays, 11am – 12pm) Lead brief sound check with student musicians prior to start of Chapel Lead Chapel Band in facilitating all music for weekly Chapel services Coordinate tear-down and storage of portable sound system and necessary equipment after Chapel Administrative Support of Chapel Band Prepare & distribute chord charts, lyric sheets, videos/audio files, etc. as needed to support student musicians (using Song Select platform) Input song selections into Planning Center Services Coordinate with RSL Student Worker for preparation of lyric slides (using ProPresenter software) Maintain, organize, and advise on purchasing of instruments, cables, and sound equipment as needed to support the ministry of Chapel Band Meet periodically with Religious & Spiritual Life Staff for planning of Chapel Services Coordinate CCLI Reporting with Religious & Spiritual Life Admin Assistant Special Chapel Worship Opportunities Organize Chapel Band in preparing to lead special worship opportunities throughout the year, including services such as Welcome Week Chapel, Family Weekend Chapel, Final Ala Cumba Memorial Service (Homecoming), Night of Worship, or other opportunities as may arise Organize Chapel Band in preparing to lead special worship opportunities throughout the year outside of campus, such as “McMurry Sundays” at local congregations, Youth Camps, Conferences, or other settings where Chapel Band is invited to lead worship as ambassadors from McMurry University Required Qualifications : Experience in worship leading and music ministry Strong interpersonal and communication skills to effectively mentor and collaborate with students Ability to organize and lead rehearsals efficiently Commitment to fostering a welcoming and inclusive worship environment Flexibility and creativity in adapting to the needs of a diverse campus community Minimum Education Requirements : Some College Hours Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree in Music, Worship Studies, or related field Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department Religious Life Employment Type Part-Time Minimum Experience Mid-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/81": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Regional Admission Counselor (Dallas-Fort Worth Region) Admissions - Abilene, Texas (Hybrid) McMurry University seeks an energetic, relationship-focused Regional Admission Counselor to serve as the University's primary recruitment representative in the Dallas-Fort Worth region. The Regional Admission Counselor will develop and maintain strategic relationships with high schools, community organizations, churches, counselors, alumni, and prospective students while managing a recruitment territory designed to increase enrollment and enhance McMurry University's visibility. This position serves as the face of McMurry University within the DFW market and is responsible for cultivating prospective students from inquiry through enrollment. Travel Required: Extensive regional travel throughout the Dallas-Fort Worth area and periodic travel through other areas in Texas and to McMurry University for university events. Essential Responsibilities: Territory Management & Recruitment Develop and execute a comprehensive territory recruitment plan for assigned DFW counties. Build and maintain relationships with high school counselors, administrators, teachers, coaches, and community leaders. Conduct and/or attend at minimum 3 high school visits, college fairs, transfer fairs, and community events per week during the school year. Identify opportunities to increase awareness and enrollment within assigned markets. Maintain regular communication with prospective students and families. Maintain membership in DARN (DFW Admissions Regional Network) Student Recruitment & Enrollment Counsel prospective students and families regarding admissions requirements, academic programs, scholarships, financial aid, campus life, and the enrollment process. Manage a recruitment funnel from inquiry through enrollment. Conduct individual appointments, virtual meetings, and group presentations. Follow up with prospective students through phone, text, email, and CRM campaigns. Assist students in completing admissions and financial aid requirements. Relationship Development Develop partnerships with high schools, community colleges, churches, homeschool organizations, and community groups. Coordinate counselor breakfasts, regional receptions, and recruitment events. Engage McMurry alumni and supporters within the DFW region to support recruitment efforts. Partner with coaches, faculty, and university representatives when appropriate. Event Support Assist with planning and execution of: Preview Events Admitted Student Days Campus Visit Programs Special Enrollment Events SOAR  - support the execution of Student Orientation and Registration between June and August. Travel to campus periodically to support major admissions initiatives. Data & Reporting Maintain accurate records within the University's CRM system. Track recruitment activity and enrollment outcomes. Analyze territory trends and recommend strategies for improvement. Submit regular reports regarding territory performance and recruitment efforts. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Valid driver's license and ability to travel extensively throughout the DFW Metroplex. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills. Strong organizational and time management abilities. Ability to work independently while contributing to a collaborative admissions team. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and CRM technology. Preferred Qualifications Previous admissions, enrollment management, recruitment, sales, marketing, or relationship-management experience. Experience in higher education. Familiarity with CRM systems such as Slate, Jenzabar, or similar platforms. Experience conducting presentations and public speaking. Bilingual in English/Spanish is highly preferred Physical Requirements Ability to travel frequently throughout assigned territory. Ability to transport recruitment materials and displays. Ability to stand for extended periods at recruitment events and college fairs. Core Competencies Relationship Building Customer Service Communication Initiative Strategic Thinking Organization Recruitment and Sales Skills Data-Informed Decision Making EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas (Hybrid) Department Admissions Employment Type Full-Time Minimum Experience Mid-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
