    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/102": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Academic Success Coach S3C - Abilene, Texas Job Summary This individual will work in support of the Warhawk Success Center (WHSC) to provide direct services to students. The Academic Coach helps students develop skills, behaviors and habits that contribute to success in college. These includes academic and career goal setting, learning strategies, time management and organization, self-regulation and self-efficacy. Job Duties and Responsibilities Fosters persistence and completion of a caseload of students Monitors progress of students in caseload with check-ins, scheduled meetings or proactive outreach and communication, responding to students questions, concerns and needs Conducts academic coaching through individual or group sessions that help students assess their own performance and develop academic success plans Assists students in developing self-efficacy by identifying and overcoming obstacles that may be impeding academic success; works with students to learn strong time management and organization skills; motivates students to practice self-regulation and take ownership of their academic success Helps students in identifying, developing and implementing learning strategies and study skills specific to course materials Refers students to appropriate academic personnel and support resources and collaborates with others to monitor and accelerate the academic progress of the students referred Performs duties that are unique to specific department or academic college Evaluate the academic progress of students completing the Academic Success Plan Maintain appropriate documentation of all meetings with students Maintain regular communication with students throughout the semester Conduct during-term and end-of-term student interventions as needed based on course performance and/or GPA Coordinate with faculty and staff to help meet students’ academic needs Connect at-risk students with appropriate academic support programming Collect, document, and provide necessary reports related to departmental goals Other duties as assigned by the Director Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree, 2-3 years of experience in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or other closely related field; • Strong time management and problem solving skills • Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite • Excellent written and communication skills • Ability to communicate with a variety of campus constituencies Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or other closely related field is preferred. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department S3C Employment Type Full-Time Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/105": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Sports Information Assistant Athletics SID - Abilene, Texas Major/Essential Duties of the Job: Coordinate department photography and videography, including headshots, team photos, media day, promo videos, and action photos. Coordinate and produce all live video streaming for all home events, as well as produce video content for the website. Create and manage content (photography, videography, and graphics) for the McMurry Athletics social media portfolio (Instagram, Facebook, X), with a specific priority on enhancing department branding initiatives. Assume other projects and duties as assigned and agreed upon by the Sports Information Director and Athletics Director. Assist in all daily operations of the Sports Information office, working under the Director of Sports Information. Serve as a secondary communications contact for other sports as needed. Assist with managing, creating, and strategizing creative digital content for the department’s social media channels for athletic game days. Coordinate media credential requests, arrange interviews for coaches, student-athletes, and staff, and handle any other media requests. Coordinate all aspects of media coverage for home events, utilizing modern technology to accommodate media productions. Support special athletic events, including the Wally Award ceremony, Jimmy Lee Pierce Golf Classic, and other events as directed by the Athletics Director and Sports Information Director. Maintain and oversee athletics media and game day equipment and manage post-event reporting and documentation requirements. Keep statistics, maintain program records, and track statistics for teams. Experience with NCAA live stats and Presto. Write features and press releases, and participate in some public address, radio, and/or video work. Help with the recruitment, training, scheduling, and supervision of student workers/assistants. Preferred Education/Experience: • Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Sports Management, Journalism, or a related field. • 2-3 years of experience in sports information, media relations, or a related role. • Proficiency with digital media tools, including web content management systems, social media platforms, and graphic design software. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department Athletics SID Employment Type Part-Time Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/107": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Postal Clerk - Part Time Post Office - Abilene, Texas Major/Essential Duties of the Job: Sign for all accountable mail. Sort and distribute all mail including campus mail. Write notification cards and get signatures for all packages. Sell stamps, money orders, etc. and assist customers as needed. Weigh and meter all outgoing mail. Charge departments for postage used & run daily postage report. Maintain accurate stamp inventory. Issue post office boxes to students and maintain filing records for post office boxes currently in use. Follow USPS Dangerous Goods and Export Compliance safety regulations. Separate and forward mail as necessary. Return mail & forward mail in accordance with USPS regulations. Run bulk mailings. Complete daily financial report (Form 1412-B) as required by USPS and deposit into USPS bank account when required. Pick up mail at the Southern Hills branch Post Office when assigned. Occasional duties: Temporary forwarding of mail in summer months. Cover Print Shop as needed. Other miscellaneous duties as assigned by Post Office Supervisor and/or Vice President of Information & Support Services. Required Education/Experience: High School Diploma/GED Basic computer skills required. Other Job requirements: Must be able to do some lifting, able to multi-task, and detail oriented. Preferred Education/Experience: At least one year of customer service experience desired or previous mail room experience. EEO Statement McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department Post Office Employment Type Part-Time Minimum Experience Mid-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://mcmurry.bamboohr.com/careers/108": {
      "title": "BambooHR",
      "description": "BambooHR Privacy Policy Job Openings Digital Media Specialist Marketing & Communications - Abilene, Texas Position Summary The Digital Media Specialist is a creative and data-informed communications professional responsible for leading the University’s social media strategy and digital storytelling efforts. This role enhances McMurry’s brand presence, supports enrollment and engagement goals, and connects with key audiences through compelling, platform-specific content. Reporting to the Director of Integrated Communications, the Specialist serves as the University’s primary social media strategist and content creator. The position collaborates closely with all members of the StratCom team to support integrated digital campaigns, ensuring messaging is cohesive, engaging, and aligned with institutional priorities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Social Media Strategy & Management Lead the development and execution of a comprehensive social media strategy aligned with University goals and brand standards. Manage and grow McMurry’s primary social media channels, ensuring consistent voice, tone, and visual identity. Plan and execute an annual and ongoing social content calendar across platforms. Expand audience reach and engagement through strategic content development and active community management. Advise campus partners on social media best practices, account creation, and platform use. Content Creation & Storytelling Create engaging, platform-specific content , including posts, photography, graphics, and short-form video , that highlights the McMurry experience. Capture and produce high-quality photo and video content, including event coverage, interviews, and campus life, and edit short-form video optimized for social platforms. Collaborate with campus partners to identify and develop compelling stories that showcase student life, academic excellence, and campus culture . E nsu re all content aligns with University brand guidelines and editorial standards. Campaign Development & Collaboration Develop and execute social media campaigns that support enrollment, advancement, and institutional initiatives. Collaborate with web and email marketing team members to support integrated, multi-channel campaigns. Provide content, messaging, and creative assets to support website and email marketing initiatives. Coordinate with internal stakeholders and external vendors to support campaign execution. Analytics & Optimization Monitor and analyze social media performance, using data to inform strategy and improve outcomes. Track key performance indicators (KPIs) including engagement, reach, and conversions. Provide regular reports and insights to internal stakeholders. Identify opportunities to optimize content and audience engagement across platforms. Core Competencies Social Media Strategy & Execution Content Creation & Storytelling Data Analysis & Performance Optimization Collaboration & Relationship Building Brand Stewardship Organizational Agility & Adaptability Judgment & Decision-Making Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in marketing , c ommunications, or related field 1–3 years of professional experience in social media or digital content creation Demonstrated experience managing social media platforms and executing campaigns Strong writing , editing, and visual storytelling skills Familiarity with social media management and analytics tools Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education marketing or communications Experience managing social media for an organization or brand Experience analyzing metrics and translating data into actionable insights Basic photography and video editing skills Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action McMurry University is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the university community and prohibits unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, national origin, age, genetic information, disability or veteran status, in employment or the provision of services, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws. Discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation is also prohibited pursuant to University policy. Apply for This Job Link to This Job Location Abilene, Texas Department Marketing & Communications Employment Type Full-Time Minimum Experience Entry-level Privacy Policy • Terms of Service • © BambooHR All rights reserved."
    }
